# Force a textual diff for every source and data format in this repo.
#
# Git decides "binary" by sniffing content, and a single control byte anywhere in
# EITHER side of a diff is enough: `encoding-properties.test.ts` carried one
# literal NUL inside an `fc.constantFrom` delimiter corpus, so `git diff` and
# GitHub both rendered the whole file as `Binary files ... differ` and `Bin 11309
# -> 12322 bytes`. A 200 -> 60 run-count cut to the `computeOrderId` escrow
# preimage properties landed inside that suppression, reviewable only under
# `git diff --text`.
#
# These files are the reviewer's only evidence. A test corpus that has to hold a
# control byte MUST spell it as an escape (`"\u0000"`, not the raw byte), and
# this file is the backstop for the case where one arrives anyway: the diff stays
# readable instead of the change going dark.
*.ts    diff
*.mts   diff
*.cts   diff
*.tsx   diff
*.js    diff
*.mjs   diff
*.cjs   diff
*.json  diff
*.md    diff
*.yml   diff
*.yaml  diff
*.nr    diff
*.toml  diff
*.sha256 diff
